  "context": "## Why Selection Cannot See It\nInsolvency, positive deviation, and a case (Nokia) in which market and evolutionary predictions pointed confidently in the wrong direction — the case that motivates the claim that the two instruments are complementary, not rival. Why selection does not refute this theory; it nests inside it.\n\nBuilds on Paper 1 ( The Map and the Flow ) and Paper 2 ( Rationality, Coherence, and the Frame ). This paper supplies the dynamics — insolvency and the closed-system destiny — and the central defense: the rival most likely to topple the theory, evolutionary / market selection, does not reach it. Nokia is the witnessed, motivating case used to show the two instruments are complementary, not rival; it is not a causal account of why any firm declined. The forward forecasts (the Outlook) and the consolidated falsification battery are deferred to later papers in the series; falsifiable claims are marked inline.\nEtiquetas: Experimentación, falsación y contraejemplos 83.33%; Cambio de perspectiva 16.67%\nFicha: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/why-selection-cannot-see-it-t1491/\nDocumento de origen: https://tegrity.ai/why-selection-cannot-see-it/\n\n",
